For explainability, our features include source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval trace, and every interaction logged for a posteriori audit. Human oversight is also built into the workflow, where the assistant proposes and the professional validates and signs.

In terms of performance, we have two model options: a Sovereign European open-weight model (self-hosted) that is fully auditable but has somewhat lower raw performance on complex tasks, and top-tier proprietary models (via API) with higher performance but lower internal transparency. The choice between these models will trade performance against explainability and sovereignty.

Our iterative methodologies involve corpus curation with the firm's experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop to ensure answer quality measured with a labelled evaluation set built with the client.

These components can help address multiple client requirements and constraints related to productivity, quality, reliability, explainability, and data sovereignty.
